  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a high average price (>85) but the model forecasts a significant decline (e.g., dropping from ~87 to <82), the true outcome almost always reverses sharply upward within 3-5 days, often exceeding the forecast by 10-15 points.",
    "The model exhibits a severe 'overshoot' bias during volatility spikes; when sentiment turns neutral or slightly positive (0.00-0.20) following a price drop, the true outcome frequently rallies to new highs rather than continuing the predicted downtrend.",
    "In periods of high historical volatility with mixed sentiment, the model's linear downward projection fails to account for mean reversion, consistently underestimating the recovery phase by 15-20% of the total range.",
    "If the last 3 days show a price decline while sentiment remains low (0.00), the true outcome typically reverses direction within the next 4-6 days, whereas the model continues its downward slope."
  ]
}
